# Root-level context: the `web` service builds from the repository root now (so its
# image can also COPY docs/ and README.md — see frontend/Dockerfile and
# docs/ADDED_REQUIREMENTS.md#37), so this is the ignore file Docker actually reads for
# that build. The per-package .dockerignore files no longer apply once the context is
# the root, and are kept only for local tooling that still expects them there.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.log
.git
backend/storage
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
